# Maintenance mode toggle.
#
# Set PUBLIC_MAINTENANCE to "true" to build the site in maintenance mode, where
# every page shows the maintenance page instead of site content. Note: this only
# affects the NEXT build — a static site must be rebuilt/redeployed to apply it.
#
# Local development: copy this file to `.env` and flip the value.
#   PUBLIC_MAINTENANCE=true
#
# Production (GitHub Pages): GitHub Pages never reads .env files. Instead, set
# the repository variable MAINTENANCE_MODE to "true" under
# Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions, then re-run the "Deploy to GitHub
# Pages" workflow (or push to main). Set it back to "false" (or delete it) and
# redeploy to restore the full site.
PUBLIC_MAINTENANCE=false